      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I think this will slowly become more necessary as VRchat grows. In a large crowd, it's difficult to notice avatars \"physically\" raising their hands, there's too much going on. When AltSpace had huge events, the raised hand also meant the hosts could pull members of the audience into the main room (I forget their terminology for this, but they had events cloned over multiple rooms).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
